---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import {designs} from '../data/jhula/designs';
import {setDirections} from '../data/jhula/sets';
import JhulaFeedback from '../components/JhulaFeedback.astro';
import additionalChoices from '../data/jhula/additional.json';
const pattachitraChoices=[
 {id:'19',name:'Ivory Flap — Pattachitra',src:'ivory-flap-pattachitra.png',width:1536,height:1024,description:'Ivory cloth, a softly rounded flap and a wooden button. Terracotta flowers and curling vines trace the flap edge and shoulder strap.'},
 {id:'20',name:'Poet’s Classic — Pattachitra',src:'poets-classic-pattachitra.png',width:1024,height:1536,description:'The familiar golden Poet’s Classic, with its open top and wooden-button closure. A flowering border runs near the hem and continues along the sling.'},
];
const groups=['01-03','04-06','07-09','10-12'];
---
<Shell title="Odia Poetry Jhula" description="A little of home, wherever words take you. Explore twenty Jhula designs, including two Pattachitra-inspired border studies, then help choose the first samples." active="explore" wide related={false} shareImage={{src:'/images/poetry-jhula/story-v2.png',alt:'Imagined scene of a woman writing and a man reading with their Jhulas nearby',width:1536,height:1024}}>
<article class="jhula wrap">
<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">ODIA POETRY JHULA · A STORY IN CLOTH</p><h1>Some things carry<br/><em>more than words.</em></h1><p class="lead">A familiar book. An unfinished poem.<br/>A little of home, wherever we go.</p><p>For women and men who read, write, listen and remember. Twenty Jhula choices: eighteen matching sets and two new Pattachitra-inspired border studies.</p><nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#story">Read the story ↓</a><a href="#collection">Explore the collection ↓</a><a href="#vote">Help us choose ↓</a><a href="#additional-choices">Additional choices ↓</a></nav><figure><img src="/images/poetry-jhula/story-v2.png" width="1536" height="1024" alt="Imagined scene of a woman writing beside a man reading, with soft cloth Jhulas resting near their chairs" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>A quiet afternoon. Two readers. A little of home between them.</figcaption></figure></header>
<div class="specs"><span>Tussar + khadi directions</span><span>90 cm finished sling</span><span>Wooden button + cloth loop</span><span>20 design choices</span></div>
<section id="story" class="poetic-story"><p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE OF HOME</p><div class="story-intro"><h2>Some roads lead back<br/>to <em>a familiar voice.</em></h2><p class="lead">Rain on the veranda. A book with softened corners.<br/>Someone reading aloud in the next room.</p></div>
<figure class="poetry-quote"><blockquote lang="or">ବିଶ୍ୱ ଦେଖ ମଧୁମୟରେ ଜୀବନ !</blockquote><figcaption>ଗଙ୍ଗାଧର ମେହେର · <cite>ମଧୁମୟ</cite>, ଅର୍ଘ୍ୟଥାଳୀ<br/><a href="https://or.wikisource.org/wiki/ଅର୍ଘ୍ୟଥାଳୀ/ମଧୁମୟ">Gangadhar Meher · Read the poem</a></figcaption></figure>
<div class="chapters"><article><span>01 / THE MORNING WE REMEMBER</span><h3>A book beside the door.</h3><p>Before the day grows busy, she takes down a book. A name on the first page, written years ago. A pressed leaf, still keeping its place. Outside, rain darkens the courtyard; inside, an old line returns in a voice she has never quite forgotten.</p><p>She slips the book into her Jhula.<br/>A little of that morning goes with her.</p></article><article><span>02 / THE ROAD THAT TAKES US AWAY</span><h3>Home, between two pages.</h3><p>In another city, he waits for a bus with a book open in his hand. Around him, the day hurries past. Then an Odia word rises from the page, and for a moment there is the veranda again—the smell of wet earth, the clink of a teacup, someone calling him inside.</p><p>The road is unfamiliar.<br/>The voice is home.</p></article><article><span>03 / THE EVENING WE BRING BACK</span><h3>One more line before we go.</h3><p>By evening, there is a table, two cups and time for one more poem. She reads; he listens. A memory loosens into a story. Someone writes a line in the margin so it will not be lost by morning.</p><p>The Jhulas rest beside their chairs.<br/>There is always room for another story.</p></article></div>
<p class="story-refrain">A book for the road.<br/>A page for what returns.<br/>A little of Odisha, close to the heart.</p>
<div class="story-purpose"><p>This is the Jhula we imagine: cloth that softens with use, a broad sling over the shoulder, room for a book and the beginnings of a poem. With a sari, a panjabi, or jeans and yesterday’s favourite tee—something familiar to carry into a new day.</p><p>Its borders look towards Odisha’s textile traditions; its purpose looks towards the hands and voices that keep them alive. We hope to bring readers, writers and local makers together, with paid work and proper credit for the people who make each piece possible.</p></div></section>
<section id="kit"><p class="eyebrow">THE POETRY KIT</p><h2>One thread.<br/><em>Six companions.</em></h2><p class="lead">The same border finds another page.<br/>The same colour keeps a pen company.</p><p>Each Jhula has its own matching Poetry Kit: the bag, an A5 cloth notebook, a refillable pen, a bookmark, a pen sleeve and an Odia poetry book to be selected. Its colour and border connect the everyday things we carry.</p><p>We intend to pay and credit makers and creators. Actual materials, partnerships, book selection and payment terms remain to be agreed.</p></section>
<section id="collection"><p class="eyebrow">TWELVE DESIGNS · TWELVE MATCHING SETS</p><h2>Find the one that <em>feels like you.</em></h2><p>Explore the first twelve matching sets, then six more sets and two new border studies below. Choose 1–5 to tell us how likely you are to buy a design. Your choice saves automatically. Leave a few words wherever a design speaks to you, and send your comments at the end.</p><p class="note">These are design studies awaiting physical sampling. The sling specification is <strong>90 cm along the exposed strap between its top attachment points</strong>, not the vertical drop. Set images interpret the bags; the bag-only views show the earlier shape, cloth and border concepts behind each matching set.</p>
<div class="designs">{designs.map((d,i)=>{const x=(i%3)*512;const [bx,by,bw,bh]=d.view.split(' ');return <article class="design" id={'design-'+d.id}><div class="design-title"><p class="eyebrow">{d.id} · {d.family==='Core'?'Core collection':d.family}</p><h3>{d.name}</h3></div><svg viewBox={x+' 0 512 1024'} role="img" aria-label={d.name+' matching Poetry Kit concept'}><defs><clipPath id={'set-'+d.id}><rect x={x} y="0" width="512" height="1024"/></clipPath></defs><image clip-path={'url(#set-'+d.id+')'} href={'/images/poetry-jhula/sets-'+groups[Math.floor(i/3)]+'-v2.png'} width="1536" height="1024"/></svg><div class="design-copy"><div class="design-description"><p class="set-line">{setDirections[d.id].line}</p><p>{setDirections[d.id].detail}</p></div><details><summary>See the bag on its own</summary><svg viewBox={d.view} role="img" aria-label={d.name+' bag-only concept'}><defs><clipPath id={'bag-'+d.id}><rect x={bx} y={by} width={bw} height={bh}/></clipPath></defs><image clip-path={'url(#bag-'+d.id+')'} href={d.src} width={d.imageWidth} height={d.imageHeight}/></svg><p>{d.detail}</p><p><strong>Cloth direction:</strong> {d.material}</p></details><JhulaFeedback id={d.id} name={d.name}/></div></article>})}</div></section>
<section id="additional-choices" class="additional-choices"><p class="eyebrow">SIX MORE DESIGNS · SIX MATCHING POETRY KITS</p><h2>More ways to <em>carry a poem.</em></h2><p>These six choices now join the vote. Each kit includes the Jhula, an A5 notebook, refillable pen, bookmark, pen sleeve and a poetry-book placeholder. Your choices save as you go. Send any comments at the end of the page.</p><div class="additional-grid">{additionalChoices.map(choice=><article class="additional-choice" id={'design-'+choice.voteId}><div class="design-title"><p class="eyebrow">{choice.voteId} · Additional collection</p><h3>{choice.name}</h3></div><svg class="additional-kit" viewBox={(choice.kitColumn*512)+' 0 512 1024'} role="img" aria-label={choice.name+' complete Poetry Kit concept'}><defs><clipPath id={'additional-kit-'+choice.voteId}><rect x={choice.kitColumn*512} y="0" width="512" height="1024"/></clipPath></defs><image clip-path={'url(#additional-kit-'+choice.voteId+')'} href={choice.kitSrc} width="1536" height="1024"/></svg><div class="design-copy"><div class="design-description"><p>{choice.description}</p></div><details><summary>See the bag on its own</summary><div class="bag-board"><img src={choice.src} width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt={choice.name+' bag design and details'}/></div></details><JhulaFeedback id={choice.voteId} name={choice.name}/></div></article>)}</div><p class="note">Matching kit studies accompany the original bag designs. Materials and illustrated dimensions await sampling; the poetry book will be selected before production.</p></section>
<section id="pattachitra-choices"><p class="eyebrow">TWO NEW BORDER STUDIES</p><h2>A little garden.<br/><em>A familiar shoulder.</em></h2><p>Pattachitra-inspired flowers and curling vines find a home on two familiar shapes. Terracotta, ivory and black bring a new rhythm to the border. Choose your stars below; your choice saves automatically.</p><div class="additional-grid">{pattachitraChoices.map(choice=><article class="additional-choice" id={'design-'+choice.id}><div class="design-title"><p class="eyebrow">{choice.id} · Pattachitra-inspired</p><h3>{choice.name}</h3></div><div class="pattachitra-image"><img src={'/images/poetry-jhula/additional/'+choice.src} width={choice.width} height={choice.height} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt={choice.description}/></div><div class="design-copy"><div class="design-description"><p>{choice.description}</p></div><JhulaFeedback id={choice.id} name={choice.name}/></div></article>)}</div><p class="note">Bag and border studies. Cloth, painting technique and colourfastness await sampling with a maker.</p></section>
<section class="styling"><p class="eyebrow">EVERYDAY POETIC ATTIRE</p><h2>A sari. A kurta.<br/><em>Whatever feels like you.</em></h2><p>The same collection belongs to whoever chooses it. Soft cloth and a familiar book can find their place in an ordinary day.</p><figure><img src="/images/poetry-jhula/women-styling.png" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" alt="Styling study showing women carrying Jhulas with a green sari and an ivory kurta"/><figcaption>Styling concept only; loaded samples will establish actual fit and comfort.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/poetry-jhula/men-styling-v2.png" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" alt="Two male styling concepts: golden Poet’s Classic with a charcoal T-shirt and jeans; ivory flap Jhula with an off-white panjabi and jeans"/><figcaption>Poet’s Classic with a T-shirt and jeans · Ivory Jhula with a panjabi and jeans.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="vote" class="vote"><p class="eyebrow">A WORD FROM YOU</p><h2>What would you<br/><em>carry with you?</em></h2><p class="lead">A favourite colour. A remembered border.<br/>A little change that would make it yours.</p><p>Your choices save automatically. If you have a thought to share, leave it here. Your words will help us choose what to make first.</p>
<form id="jhula-feedback" data-storage="firebase">
<fieldset data-feedback-fields disabled><legend>Your note to us</legend><label class="form-field">Your thoughts <span>(optional · up to 1,000 characters)</span><textarea name="comment" maxlength="1000" rows="5" placeholder="Tell us what stays with you—a colour, a memory, or something you would change…"></textarea></label>
<fieldset class="kit-preference"><legend>What would you carry?</legend>{[['bag','Just the Jhula'],['kit','The Poetry Kit'],['unsure','Still imagining']].map(([value,label])=><label><input type="radio" name="kit" value={value} checked={value==='unsure'}/>{label}</label>)}</fieldset>
<label class="form-field">Your name <span>(required to send your note)</span><input name="name" maxlength="80" autocomplete="name" required/></label>
<fieldset class="contact-fields"><legend>A way to write back</legend><p class="note" id="contact-help">Please leave either your email or your phone number, so we can get back to you.</p><div class="contact-grid"><label class="form-field">Email<input type="email" name="email" maxlength="254" autocomplete="email" aria-describedby="contact-help"/></label><label class="form-field">Phone<input type="tel" name="phone" maxlength="40" autocomplete="tel" aria-describedby="contact-help"/></label></div></fieldset>
<p class="note">Your comments and contact details are shared only with the Project Odisha team.</p><button class="vote-button" type="submit" id="save-ratings">Send my comments</button><p id="comments-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>
<p id="rating-summary" aria-live="polite"></p><button type="button" id="clear-favourite" class="clear-rating">Clear favourite choice</button>
<p id="ratings-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="ratings-error" role="alert" hidden></p><button type="button" id="retry-ratings" hidden>Try again</button><div id="withdraw-area" hidden><button type="button" id="withdraw-ratings">Withdraw my response</button><div id="withdraw-confirm" hidden><p>Remove your saved choices and comments? This cannot be undone.</p><button type="button" id="confirm-withdraw">Yes, withdraw my response</button><button type="button" id="cancel-withdraw">Keep my response</button></div></div>
<noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to save your choices and comments on this page.</p></noscript>
</form></section>

<details class="credits"><summary>About the concepts and craft inspiration</summary><p>Contemporary original concept studies inspired by Odisha’s textile vocabulary, not verified historical reproductions or certified craft products. No maker partnership or finished product is claimed.</p><p>Puri directions draw on Pipili appliqué and Raghurajpur painting. Katak linework translates Tarakasi into proposed embroidery, not silver. Western Odisha studies start with Sambalpur–Bargarh weaving references and do not represent every regional tradition.</p><p>Books are placeholders; title and edition remain unselected. Fabric, dimensions, colourfastness, construction, fit and price need physical sampling.</p><p>Craft background: <a href="https://odishatourism.gov.in/en/arts-crafts-handloom">Odisha Tourism</a> · <a href="https://eodbodisha.odisha.gov.in/Upload/ODOP/Prod_Desc/Sambalpur.pdf">Sambalpur district profile</a>.</p></details>
<p class="return"><a href="/literature/">Continue into Odia literature →</a></p>
</article>
</Shell>
<script>
import '../scripts/jhula-feedback';
</script>
<style>
.pattachitra-image{position:relative;aspect-ratio:1;background:#f6edda;flex-shrink:0}.jhula .pattachitra-image img{position:absolute;inset:0;display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain}#pattachitra-choices .design-description{flex:1}#pattachitra-choices>.note{margin-top:24px}

.jhula{padding-bottom:64px}.jhula section{padding-block:56px;scroll-margin-top:100px}
.jhula h1,.jhula h2,.jhula h3,.jhula p{margin:0}.jhula h2{font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,58px);line-height:1.16;margin-bottom:24px}.jhula h3{font-size:clamp(24px,2.2vw,28px);line-height:1.25}.jhula em{color:var(--sea)}.jhula p{line-height:1.75;max-width:920px}.jhula p+p{margin-top:12px}.jhula .eyebrow{line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:16px}.lead{font-size:clamp(20px,2.3vw,28px)}.jhula .lead+p{margin-top:20px}
.hero{display:block;padding:40px 0 0}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(42px,7vw,100px);line-height:1.07;margin:16px 0 24px;max-width:1000px}.hero>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:760px}.hero nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 28px;margin:20px 0 24px}.hero nav a,.return a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;box-sizing:border-box}
.jhula figure{margin:28px 0 0}.jhula figure img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.hero figure img{max-height:700px;object-fit:cover}.jhula figcaption,.note{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.jhula figcaption{padding-top:12px;line-height:1.6}.specs{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 28px;border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding:20px 0;margin-top:28px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5}
.story-intro{max-width:850px}.chapters{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px;margin-top:40px}.chapters article>span{font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--earth)}.chapters h3{margin:12px 0 16px}.story-purpose{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:32px}.story-purpose p+p{margin:0}.jhula .poetry-quote{text-align:center;padding:28px 16px;border-block:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:32px}.poetry-quote blockquote{font-family:Georgia,serif;margin:8px 0 16px;font-size:clamp(27px,4vw,46px);line-height:1.9}.poetry-quote figcaption{padding:0;line-height:1.8}.jhula .story-refrain{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,40px);text-align:center;margin:44px auto;line-height:1.6;color:var(--sea)}
#kit{border-block:1px solid var(--line)}
.designs,.additional-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:28px;margin-top:28px;align-items:stretch}.additional-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}
.design,.additional-choice{display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--paper);min-width:0;overflow:hidden}
.design-title{padding:24px;box-sizing:border-box;min-height:140px}.design-title .eyebrow{margin-bottom:12px}.design-title h3{margin:0}
.design>svg,.additional-kit{display:block;width:100%;height:440px;background:var(--paper);flex-shrink:0}.additional-kit{height:560px}
.design-copy{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px;padding:24px;flex:1;min-width:0}.design-description p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.7}.design-description .set-line{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.5}.design-description p+p{margin-top:12px}
.design-copy>details{margin-top:auto;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.design-copy>details>summary{cursor:pointer;padding:12px 0;min-height:44px;box-sizing:border-box;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5}.design-copy>details svg{display:block;width:100%;height:370px}.design-copy>details p{font-size:14px;margin-top:12px}.bag-board{aspect-ratio:1536/910;overflow:hidden;margin-top:8px}.bag-board img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}
.additional-choices{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.additional-choices>.note{margin-top:24px}.styling{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.styling figure+figure{margin-top:32px}
.vote{max-width:820px;margin-inline:auto}.vote .lead{margin-bottom:20px}#jhula-feedback{margin-top:28px}#jhula-feedback>fieldset{border:0;padding:0;margin:0;min-width:0}#jhula-feedback>fieldset>legend{padding:0;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:24px}.form-field{display:block;margin:0 0 24px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5}.form-field span{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.form-field textarea,.form-field input{display:block;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;background:#fffdf8;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;padding:12px;font:inherit;line-height:1.6;margin-top:8px;resize:vertical;min-height:48px}
.kit-preference{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:12px 20px 16px;margin:0 0 24px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 24px;min-width:0}.kit-preference legend{padding:0 6px;font-size:15px}.kit-preference label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:44px;line-height:1.5;font-size:14px}.kit-preference input{width:18px;height:18px;margin:0;accent-color:var(--sea);flex-shrink:0}
.contact-fields{border:0;padding:0;margin:0 0 8px;min-width:0}.contact-fields legend{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:22px;line-height:1.3;padding:0;margin-bottom:12px}.contact-fields>.note{margin-bottom:16px}.contact-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}.contact-grid .form-field{margin:0 0 16px}
.vote-button{display:inline-block;background:var(--sea);color:white;padding:16px 24px;text-decoration:none;margin:20px 0 0;font-weight:600;min-height:48px}.clear-rating{display:block;background:none;border:0;text-decoration:underline;color:var(--sea);cursor:pointer;padding:10px 0;min-height:44px;font-size:13px;text-align:left}#save-ratings{border:0;cursor:pointer;font:inherit}#save-ratings:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:wait}.vote fieldset:disabled{opacity:.65}#ratings-status,#comments-status,#rating-summary{font-size:14px;margin-top:16px}#ratings-status:empty,#comments-status:empty,#rating-summary:empty{display:none}#ratings-error{padding:16px;margin-top:16px;border-left:3px solid #9b3624;color:#842817;background:#fff2ed}#retry-ratings,#withdraw-ratings,#confirm-withdraw,#cancel-withdraw{padding:12px 16px;min-height:44px;margin:8px 12px 0 0;border:1px solid var(--sea);background:transparent;color:var(--sea);cursor:pointer}#withdraw-confirm{padding:16px;background:var(--paper);margin-top:12px}
.credits{border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding:12px 0}.credits summary{cursor:pointer;padding:12px 0;min-height:44px;box-sizing:border-box}.credits p{font-size:14px;margin:12px 0}.jhula .return{margin-top:24px}.jhula a:focus-visible,.jhula summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--earth);outline-offset:4px}
@media(max-width:1100px){.designs{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.chapters{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:32px}.chapters article{max-width:760px}.story-purpose{gap:24px}.design-title{min-height:136px}}
@media(max-width:720px){.designs,.additional-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.design-title{min-height:0;padding:20px}.design-copy{padding:20px}.design>svg,.additional-kit{height:auto;aspect-ratio:1/1.65;max-height:650px}.story-purpose{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:20px}.hero figure img{max-height:none}.jhula section{padding-block:40px}.hero{padding-top:28px}.hero nav{gap:0 20px}.specs{font-size:12px;gap:10px 20px}.contact-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0}.poetry-quote{padding-inline:0}.jhula .story-refrain{margin-block:32px}.jhula h2{margin-bottom:20px}.kit-preference{padding-inline:16px}}
</style>
